    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Goal\nImplement the backend contract for the Import as project onboarding flow. This is the shared foundation that workspace import will extend.\n\n## Scope\n- Add POST /imports/validate for importKind: project.\n- Validate the selected folder without mutating Git or the filesystem.\n- Return the shared ImportValidationResult DTO with isValid, blockingErrors, root, optional childRepos, and nextStep.\n- Populate root Git state: isRepo, hasCommit, hasOrigin, isEmptyFolder, needsGitInit, requiredActions, and blockingErrors.\n- When the root is not Git-initialized but direct child repositories exist, return childRepos and nextStep: choose_import_kind. This is informational; project preparation must not modify child repositories.\n- Add POST /imports/prepare-git.\n- Require explicit approval for every requested action.\n- Execute only missing approved actions, strictly in order: git_init, then git_commit, then set_remote.\n- Do not overwrite an existing origin automatically.\n- Return or stream GitPreparationEvent values with pending, running, success, and error states.\n\n## Shared DTO Direction\n- RepoGitStatus includes repoPath, isRepo, hasCommit, hasOrigin, isEmptyFolder, needsGitInit, requiredActions, and blockingErrors.\n- ImportValidationResult includes importKind, isValid, blockingErrors, root, childRepos, and nextStep: error | choose_import_kind | prepare_git | continue.\n- Keep this contract reusable for workspace import, where childRepos carries each direct child repository's status.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- A non-Git folder requires git_init, git_commit, and set_remote.\n- A Git repository with no commit and no origin requires only git_commit and set_remote.\n- A Git repository with a commit but no origin requires only set_remote.\n- Invalid or unreadable folders return isValid: false with user-displayable blocking errors.\n- A non-Git root with child repositories returns the workspace suggestion state without mutating children.\n- Tests cover the scenarios above, plus rejected unapproved actions.\n- Regenerate OpenAPI and frontend API types.\n\n## Related\n- Workspace UX/remediation context: https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/issues/3686",
